.title 15 dB coupler with end capacitors on JLC RO4350B 0.508 mm (5 GHz), for comparison with finger loading (#41)
# A capacitor across the gap at each end of the coupled section gives the odd mode the extra capacitance that
# fingers spread along it (worked example 14, section 6). W, S and Cc from tools/capcoupler.mjs design. 48 fF is
# below any chip capacitor: in practice a printed gap or interdigital capacitor, held to about ±20 %. The coupler
# layout template does not place the capacitors; tools/capcoupler.mjs gen builds the openEMS case.
.freq 1G 9G 801
.ref 5G
.substrate jlc-ro4350b-0.508
.param w = 1.0046mm
.param s = 0.3124mm
.param cc = 0.0484p tune 0.02p 0.1p
port in    # 1
port thru  # 2
port cpl   # 3
port iso   # 4
cline K geom=msl W=w S=s
  len 90deg
  A in   cpl
  B thru iso
end
Cc1 in cpl cc
Cc2 thru iso cc
.goal db(S31) = -15 4.5G 5.5G
.plot ylim=-60,0 db(S11) db(S21) db(S31) db(S41)
.plot title=Directivity_(dB) db(S31/S41)
